Scenario 1. 1 consumer in a consumer group
set-up: [tpoic: 1, partition: 4, consumer-group: 1, consumer: 1]
result: the single consumer will read message from the  4 partitions.
        order is maintain in each partition but not across the partitions.

Scenario 2. Number of consumer in a consumer group is less than or equal the number of partition
set-up: [tpoic: 1, partition: 4, consumer-group: 1, consumer: 2]
result: the two or more consumer will read message from the  different partitions.
        broker will distribute the partition equally.
        e.g consumer-1 will read from partition 0 and 2 and consumer-2 will read from partition 1 and 3
        order is maintain in each partition but not across the partitions.

        Note: kafka assign consumers in a consumer group to a unique partition. so that each partition is
        consumer by exactly one consumer in a consumer group.
        this is to ensure that a message is ever read by a single consumer in the consumer group.

Scenario 3. Number of consumer in a consumer group is more than the number of partition
set-up: [tpoic: 1, partition: 4, consumer-group: 1, consumer: 5]
result: four out of the five consumer will read message from single partitions each.
        broker will assign a partition to four of the consumer.
        e.g consumer-1 will read from partition 0, consumer-2 will read from partiton 2, consumer-3 will read from partiton 3, and consumer-4 will read from partiton 1
        order is maintain in each partition but not across the partitions.

